  "id": "geneenvironment-interaction",
  "term": "gene–environment interaction",
  "definition": "Gene–environment interaction is the combined influence of genetic vulnerability and environmental vulnerability on how substance use patterns or substance use disorders emerge. In this context, it refers to how gene-related factors and life circumstances may work together, although reported findings have been mixed.",
